### Prisma Nominations API — ejemplos (IntelliJ HTTP Client)
# Datos ficticios. card_id es siempre un token, nunca un PAN.
# Correr en orden: E1 guarda el id y la URI de la nominación para los GET.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@entity = ENT01
@otherEntity = ENT02

### E1 — alta válida: 202 + Location + Idempotent-Replayed: false
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}
X-Correlation-Id: demo-e1-0001

{
  "request_id": "0b4a9f2e-6c1d-4e7a-8b3f-5d2c1a0e9f87",
  "customer_id": "CUST-000123",
  "account_id": "0001234567890987654",
  "card_id": "tok_4f9a2c7b8d1e",
  "alias": "CUENTA SUELDO"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("nominationId", response.body.nomination_id);
    client.global.set("location", response.headers.valueOf("Location"));
%}

### Consultar estado (GET por Location)
GET {{baseUrl}}{{location}}
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}

### Consultar historial
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations/{{nominationId}}/history
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}

### E3 — replay: mismo POST → 202, mismo nomination_id, Idempotent-Replayed: true
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}
X-Correlation-Id: demo-e3-0001

{
  "request_id": "0b4a9f2e-6c1d-4e7a-8b3f-5d2c1a0e9f87",
  "customer_id": "CUST-000123",
  "account_id": "0001234567890987654",
  "card_id": "tok_4f9a2c7b8d1e",
  "alias": "CUENTA SUELDO"
}

### E3 — conflicto: mismo request_id con otro contenido → 409 IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}

{
  "request_id": "0b4a9f2e-6c1d-4e7a-8b3f-5d2c1a0e9f87",
  "customer_id": "CUST-000123",
  "account_id": "0001234567890987654",
  "card_id": "tok_otra_tarjeta",
  "alias": "CUENTA SUELDO"
}

### E3 — mismo request_id en otra entidad → nominación nueva (la clave es por entidad)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Entity-Id: {{otherEntity}}

{
  "request_id": "0b4a9f2e-6c1d-4e7a-8b3f-5d2c1a0e9f87",
  "customer_id": "CUST-000123",
  "account_id": "0001234567890987654",
  "card_id": "tok_4f9a2c7b8d1e",
  "alias": "CUENTA SUELDO"
}

### Aislamiento — otra entidad consulta la nominación → 404 NOMINATION_NOT_FOUND
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations/{{nominationId}}
X-Entity-Id: {{otherEntity}}

### E2 — faltan campos obligatorios → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (errors en snake_case)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}

{
  "alias": "CUENTA SUELDO"
}

### E2 — card_id con forma de PAN → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (el valor no se devuelve)
# 4111111111111111 es el número de prueba público de Visa, no una tarjeta real.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}

{
  "request_id": "5e8c1f3a-2b7d-4c9e-a1f0-3d6b8e2c4a71",
  "customer_id": "CUST-000123",
  "account_id": "0001234567890987654",
  "card_id": "4111111111111111"
}

### E2 — JSON inválido → 400 MALFORMED_REQUEST
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}

{ "request_id": "no-es-un-uuid", "customer_id": "CUST-000123",

### E2 — falta X-Entity-Id → 400 MISSING_HEADER
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "request_id": "9a3d7e1b-4f2c-4b8a-9e6d-1c5f7a2b8d30",
  "customer_id": "CUST-000123",
  "account_id": "0001234567890987654",
  "card_id": "tok_4f9a2c7b8d1e"
}

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Integración con ABM (simulador, ver docs/abm-mock.md). El escenario se elige por el card_id.
# Cada POST usa un request_id nuevo ({{$uuid}}): se puede repetir. La respuesta de ABM llega a los
# ~2 s (nominations.abm-mock.response-delay): el GET inmediato muestra RECEIVED o PENDING_ABM.

### E4 — ABM aprueba
# Estado final: APPROVED. Historial RECEIVED → PENDING_ABM → APPROVED.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}
X-Correlation-Id: demo-e4-0001

{
  "request_id": "{{$uuid}}",
  "customer_id": "CUST-000123",
  "account_id": "0001234567890987654",
  "card_id": "tok_demo_ok_01",
  "alias": "CUENTA SUELDO"
}

> {% client.global.set("e4Id", response.body.nomination_id); %}

### E4 — estado (repetir hasta ver el estado final)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations/{{e4Id}}
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}

### E4 — historial
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations/{{e4Id}}/history
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}

### E5 — ABM rechaza (REJECT_030)
# Estado final: REJECTED con rejection_reason CARD_NOT_ELIGIBLE (el código ABM-030 no se expone).
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}
X-Correlation-Id: demo-e5-0001

{
  "request_id": "{{$uuid}}",
  "customer_id": "CUST-000123",
  "account_id": "0001234567890987654",
  "card_id": "tok_demo_REJECT_030",
  "alias": "CUENTA SUELDO"
}

> {% client.global.set("e5Id", response.body.nomination_id); %}

### E5 — estado (repetir hasta ver el estado final)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations/{{e5Id}}
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}

### E5b — ABM rechaza sin sufijo
# Estado final: REJECTED con rejection_reason ACCOUNT_BLOCKED (ABM-051 por defecto).
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}
X-Correlation-Id: demo-e5b-0001

{
  "request_id": "{{$uuid}}",
  "customer_id": "CUST-000123",
  "account_id": "0001234567890987654",
  "card_id": "tok_demo_REJECT_01",
  "alias": "CUENTA SUELDO"
}

> {% client.global.set("e5bId", response.body.nomination_id); %}

### E5b — estado (repetir hasta ver el estado final)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations/{{e5bId}}
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}

### E7 — ABM responde dos veces (DUP)
# Estado final: APPROVED. Una sola transición a APPROVED y un solo nomination.result (ver historial).
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}
X-Correlation-Id: demo-e7-0001

{
  "request_id": "{{$uuid}}",
  "customer_id": "CUST-000123",
  "account_id": "0001234567890987654",
  "card_id": "tok_demo_DUP_01",
  "alias": "CUENTA SUELDO"
}

> {% client.global.set("e7Id", response.body.nomination_id); %}

### E7 — estado (repetir hasta ver el estado final)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations/{{e7Id}}
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}

### E7 — historial (una sola fila con to_status APPROVED)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations/{{e7Id}}/history
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# E6 — Resiliencia (ver README, sección "Resiliencia (E6)", y docs/operations.md).
# Tiempos por defecto: capa 1 = 3 intentos con read-timeout 2s; capa 2 = tópicos de retry 10s, 1m y 5m;
# SLA de respuesta de ABM = 15m (sweeper cada 30s). Para verlo rápido, arrancar la app con, p.ej.:
#   mvn spring-boot:run -Dspring-boot.run.arguments="--nominations.abm.adapter.retry-delays=2s,2s --nominations.abm.sweeper.response-sla=30s"

### Estado del circuit breaker de ABM (components.circuitBreakers.details.abm.details.state)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

### E6-FAIL — ABM no disponible (503 siempre)
# RECEIVED mientras reintenta: 3 intentos por pasada × (principal, -retry-0, -retry-1, -retry-2), ~6 min con los
# defaults. Agotado → nomination.requested.v1-dlt y ABM_TIMEOUT ("Reintentos agotados: ABM no disponible"), sin
# nomination.result. Un solo FAIL ya hace hasta 12 llamadas (4 pasadas × 3): pasada la 10ª con ≥ 50 % de fallas el
# circuit breaker se abre (ver /actuator/health) y las pasadas siguientes fallan sin llamar a ABM.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}
X-Correlation-Id: demo-fail-0001

{
  "request_id": "{{$uuid}}",
  "customer_id": "CUST-000123",
  "account_id": "0001234567890987654",
  "card_id": "tok_demo_FAIL_01",
  "alias": "CUENTA SUELDO"
}

> {% client.global.set("failId", response.body.nomination_id); %}

### E6-FAIL — estado (RECEIVED mientras reintenta; luego ABM_TIMEOUT)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations/{{failId}}
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}

### E6-FAIL — historial (RECEIVED → ABM_TIMEOUT, source ABM_ADAPTER)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations/{{failId}}/history
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}

### E6-FAIL — reprocesar cuando esté en ABM_TIMEOUT (vuelve a fallar mientras ABM siga caído)
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/v1/nominations/{{failId}}/reprocess
X-Correlation-Id: demo-fail-reprocess-0001

### E6-SLOW — ABM tarda 10s en contestar el HTTP (> read-timeout 2s)
# Cada intento corta por timeout → reintentos → ABM_TIMEOUT. Pero ABM sí recibió el pedido y aprueba: la respuesta
# tardía lleva la nominación de ABM_TIMEOUT a APPROVED y se publica UN solo nomination.result.
# (Con los defaults la respuesta llega a los ~10s, antes de agotar la capa 2: se ve RECEIVED → APPROVED. Para ver
# ABM_TIMEOUT → APPROVED, acortar retry-delays como se indica arriba y subir nominations.abm-mock.slow-http-delay.)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}
X-Correlation-Id: demo-slow-0001

{
  "request_id": "{{$uuid}}",
  "customer_id": "CUST-000123",
  "account_id": "0001234567890987654",
  "card_id": "tok_demo_SLOW_01",
  "alias": "CUENTA SUELDO"
}

> {% client.global.set("slowId", response.body.nomination_id); %}

### E6-SLOW — historial
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations/{{slowId}}/history
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}

### E6-SILENT — ABM acepta (202) y nunca responde
# PENDING_ABM hasta que vence el SLA (15m); el sweeper la pasa a ABM_TIMEOUT (source SWEEPER).
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}
X-Correlation-Id: demo-silent-0001

{
  "request_id": "{{$uuid}}",
  "customer_id": "CUST-000123",
  "account_id": "0001234567890987654",
  "card_id": "tok_demo_SILENT_01",
  "alias": "CUENTA SUELDO"
}

> {% client.global.set("silentId", response.body.nomination_id); %}

### E6-SILENT — estado (PENDING_ABM; ABM_TIMEOUT pasado el SLA)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations/{{silentId}}
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}

### E6-SILENT — reproceso por un operador (solo desde ABM_TIMEOUT: 202 y RECEIVED; si no, 409 INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION)
# Sin X-Entity-Id: endpoint interno. ABM es idempotente: devuelve el mismo abm_operation_id y vuelve a PENDING_ABM.
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/v1/nominations/{{silentId}}/reprocess
X-Correlation-Id: demo-silent-reprocess-0001

### E6-SILENT — historial (… → ABM_TIMEOUT [SWEEPER] → RECEIVED [OPERATOR] → PENDING_ABM)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations/{{silentId}}/history
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}
